        "sprite_id": "info_sign",
        "label": "About this arcade"
      },
      "interaction": {
        "type": "read",
        "label": "About this arcade",
        "markdown": "## Welcome to the *arcade*.\n\nFive cabinets. Each wired to a real running thing.\n\nClick a cabinet to play the game inline. Click the speaker to hear what's playing. Click this sign. You already did.\n\n### How it works\n\nEvery sprite in your canvas can be wired to one of four interactions:\n\n- **Click-to-launch** loads a sandboxed iframe with a real app inside.\n- **Click-to-link** opens a URL in a new tab.\n- **Click-to-embed** shows an inline media player, such as YouTube, Vimeo, SoundCloud, or Bandcamp.\n- **Click-to-read** opens a long-form panel like this one.\n\n### Customize this\n\nIn Phase A.3, edit mode lets you drag sprites onto your stage, wire them to your own URLs, and ask Claude to author new components. Until then, this preset is your demo.\n\n*Linktree is a list of links. Endenza is a place.*"
      },
